  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Computational Neuroscience · Machine Learning · Bioinformatics</p>
        <h1>Dr. Lydia Moreno</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Associate Professor at Riverbend University studying how neural circuits encode and process complex sensory information.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="publications.html">View Publications</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">Contact Me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="profile-card" aria-label="Profile summary">
        <div class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">LM</div>
        <h2>Research Profile</h2>
        <p>School of Biological Sciences<br />Riverbend University</p>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Office</dt><dd>Blakely Hall, Room 312</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/lydia-moreno" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/lydia-moreno</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="section two-column" id="about">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">About Me</p>
        <h2>Building interpretable tools for modern neuroscience.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rich-text">
        <p>Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University’s School of Biological Sciences. Her work sits at the intersection of machine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics.</p>
        <p>She received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging analysis at Northborough Research Center.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Research Interests</p>
        <h2>Focus areas</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Neural Encoding & Decoding</h3>
          <p>Developing interpretable models that translate spike-train data into behavioral predictions.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Biomedical Imaging</h3>
          <p>Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to MRI and two-photon microscopy data.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Single-Cell Omics</h3>
          <p>Designing scalable pipelines for multi-modal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Explainable AI</h3>
          <p>Building frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in black-box models.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section highlighted">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Selected Projects</p>
        <h2>Recent work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article>
          <span>Lead Developer & Project Coordinator</span>
          <h3>DeepVision: High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping</h3>
          <p>A PyTorch-based pipeline for segmenting two-photon images and decoding stimulus orientation from calcium-imaging traces.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Principal Investigator</span>
          <h3>NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis</h3>
          <p>Graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Co-Principal Investigator</span>
          <h3>CellMap: Multi-Modal Single-Cell Atlas</h3>
          <p>A Nextflow workflow integrating scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data for cortical organoid analysis.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split-cards">
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="section-kicker">Teaching & Mentorship</p>
        <h2>Training the next generation of computational biologists.</h2>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Introduction to Computational Neuroscience (Spring 2025)</li>
          <li>Advanced Machine Learning Methods in Biology (Fall 2024)</li>
          <li>Supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master’s theses</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="panel dark-panel">
        <p class="section-kicker">Skills & Tools</p>
        <h2>Technical toolkit</h2>
        <p>Python, R, C++, PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, NetworkX, Nextflow, Snakemake, Docker, Kubernetes, MATLAB, Jupyter, Seurat, Scanpy, D3.js, Plotly, and Matplotlib.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>

