    <section class="section highlighted" id="interpretable-deep-learning">
      <p class="section-kicker">Featured note</p>
      <h2>Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience</h2>
      <p>Interpretability is most useful when it supports a concrete experimental loop: identify features, generate hypotheses, validate with perturbation or imaging, and refine the model. My group focuses on making that loop practical for calcium imaging, spike-train analysis, and multi-modal biological datasets.</p>
